## Original Content
Voters in at least six states will soon decide ballot measures related to voter ID — the largest number of voter ID measures in a single year. The tally includes three prominent swing states.

## Summary
This year, at least six states will decide on ballot measures related to voter ID, marking the largest number of such measures in a single year. Among these, three are prominent swing states, which could have broader political implications.

## Key Points
- At least six states will have voter ID ballot measures this year.
- This is the highest number of voter ID measures in a single year on record.
- Three of the states involved are key swing states, potentially affecting national politics.


